---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import InstallBar from '../components/InstallBar.astro';
import McpButton from '../components/McpButton.astro';
import { SITE } from '../content/nav';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
---

<DocsLayout
	title="For LLMs & agents"
	eyebrow="[ LLM · COPY ]"
	description="Machine-readable documentation so coding agents can install, run, and explain Kuyfi without inventing APIs."
>
	<div class="llm-actions">
		<a class="pill" href={withBase('/llms.txt')}>llms.txt</a>
		<a class="pill" href={withBase('/llms-full.txt')}>llms-full.txt</a>
		<McpButton href={withBase('/mcp')} />
	</div>

	<Callout type="tip" title="Preferred ingestion order">
		<ol>
			<li>Fetch <code>{SITE.url}/docs/llms.txt</code> for a compact project card.</li>
			<li>Fetch <code>{SITE.url}/docs/llms-full.txt</code> for the full operator manual.</li>
			<li>Only then open human HTML pages if you need diagrams or navigation.</li>
		</ol>
	</Callout>

	<h2>One-paragraph project card (copy)</h2>
	<pre><code>Kuyfi (@kuyfi/kuyfi, CLI `kuyfi`) is an open-source black-box security terminal for Soroban smart contracts on Stellar Testnet. Given a Contract ID, it fetches on-chain WASM, reconstructs the attack surface from contractspecv0, runs type-aware Chaos Monkey fuzzing (simulate-first, optional Testnet broadcast with ephemeral Friendbot keys), classifies DiagnosticEvent traces into a six-signal taxonomy, and exports a SecurityReport as JSON/PDF. It is not a formal audit. Testnet only. Never fuzz unauthorized contracts.</code></pre>

	<h2>Install copy for agents</h2>
	<InstallBar />

	<h2>Safe agent playbook</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>Confirm the user owns the Contract ID or has written authorization.</li>
		<li>Confirm network is Testnet (Kuyfi hardcodes Testnet RPC).</li>
		<li>
			Prefer headless: <code>kuyfi &lt;ID&gt; --json</code> for structured output.
		</li>
		<li>
			Treat <code>POTENTIAL_VULN</code> as investigate-first; never rewrite findings into
			“confirmed CVE”.
		</li>
		<li>Do not invent Mainnet support, SaaS dashboards, or MCP tools that are not shipped.</li>
	</ol>

	<h2>Prompt stub</h2>
	<pre><code>You are helping with Kuyfi, a Soroban black-box security CLI.
Rules:
- Use only documented commands from https://kuyfi.vercel.app/docs/llms-full.txt
- Testnet only; no mainnet advice that implies Kuyfi supports it
- Findings = signals, not proven exploits
- Suggest `kuyfi &lt;CONTRACT_ID&gt; --json` for CI
- Point humans to https://kuyfi.vercel.app/docs for deep pages</code></pre>

	<h2>Structured facts agents often get wrong</h2>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Fact</th>
				<th>Truth</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td>Package name</td>
				<td><code>@kuyfi/kuyfi</code> (command <code>kuyfi</code>)</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Network</td>
				<td>Stellar Testnet only</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Source required?</td>
				<td>No — WASM / contractspec on-chain</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>HTTP API</td>
				<td>Optional paid OSINT scan only; no remote Chaos Monkey</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Report schema</td>
				<td><code>schemaVersion: "1.0.0"</code></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Tagline</td>
				<td>Before the Breach.</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2>MCP</h2>
	<p>
		A Model Context Protocol surface is reserved for a later release. Use the
		<a href={withBase('/mcp')}>MCP page</a> and header <strong>MCP Connect</strong> button as the
		stable entry point once a server ships — config shape is documented there as a stub.
	</p>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
	.llm-actions {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.65rem;
		align-items: center;
		margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
	}

	.pill {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		color: var(--text);
		text-decoration: none;
		background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
	}

	.pill:hover {
		border-color: var(--yellow);
		color: var(--yellow);
		text-decoration: none;
	}
</style>
